.Sh DESCRIPTION
These functions provide compression support for OpenSSL. Compression is
used within the OpenSSL library to support TLS record and certificate
compression.
.Pp
.Fn COMP_CTX_new
is used to create a new
.Vt COMP_CTX
structure used to compress data.
.Pp
.Fn COMP_CTX_free
is used to free the returned
.Vt COMP_CTX .
If the argument is NULL, nothing is done.
.Pp
.Fn COMP_CTX_get_method
returns the
.Vt COMP_METHOD
of the given
.Fa ctx .
.Pp
.Fn COMP_CTX_get_type
and
.Fn COMP_get_type
return the NID for the
.Vt COMP_CTX
and
.Vt COMP_METHOD ,
respectively.
.Fn COMP_get_name
returns the name of the algorithm of the given
.Vt COMP_METHOD .
.Pp
.Fn COMP_compress_block
compresses b<ilen> bytes from the buffer
.Fa in
into the buffer b<out> of size
.Fa olen
using the algorithm specified by
.Fa ctx .
.Pp
.Fn COMP_expand_block
expands
.Fa ilen
bytes from the buffer
.Fa in
into the buffer
.Fa out
of size
.Fa olen
using the algorithm specified by
.Fa ctx .
.Pp
Methods
.Pf ( Vt COMP_METHOD )
may be specified by one of these functions.
These functions will be available even if their corresponding
compression algorithm is not configured into the OpenSSL library.
In such a case, NULL will be returned.
.Bl -bullet
.It
.Fn COMP_zlib
returns a
.Vt COMP_METHOD
for stream-based ZLIB compression.
.It
.Fn COMP_zlib_oneshot
returns a
.Vt COMP_METHOD
for one-shot ZLIB compression.
.It
.Fn COMP_brotli
returns a
.Vt COMP_METHOD
for stream-based Brotli compression.
.It
.Fn COMP_brotli_oneshot
returns a
.Vt COMP_METHOD
for one-shot Brotli compression.
.It
.Fn COMP_zstd
returns a
.Vt COMP_METHOD
for stream-based Zstandard compression.
.It
.Fn COMP_zstd_oneshot
returns a
.Vt COMP_METHOD
for one-shot Zstandard compression.
.El
.Pp
.Fn BIO_f_zlib ,
.Fn BIO_f_brotli
.Fn BIO_f_zstd
each return a
.Sy BIO_METHOD
that may be used to create a
.Sy BIO
via
.Sy BIO_new(3)
to read and write compressed files or streams.
The functions are only available if the corresponding algorithm is
compiled into the OpenSSL library.
NULL may be returned if the algorithm fails to load dynamically.
.Sh NOTES
While compressing non-compressible data, the output may be larger than
the input.
Care should be taken to size output buffers appropriate for both
compression and expansion.
.Pp
Compression support and compression algorithms must be enabled and built
into the library before use.
Refer to the INSTALL.md file when configuring OpenSSL.
.Pp
ZLIB may be found at
.Lk https://zlib.net
.Pp
Brotli may be found at
.Lk https://github.com/google/brotli .
.Pp
Zstandard may be found at
.Lk https://github.com/facebook/zstd .
.Pp
Compression of SSL/TLS records is not recommended, as it has been shown
to lead to the CRIME attack
.Lk https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/CRIME .
It is disabled by default, and may be enabled by clearing the
SSL_OP_NO_COMPRESSION option and setting the security level as
appropriate.
See the documentation for the
.Xr SSL_CTX_set_options 3
and
.Xr SSL_set_options 3
functions.
.Pp
Compression is also used to support certificate compression as described
in RFC8879
.Lk https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc8879 .
It may be disabled via the SSL_OP_NO_TX_CERTIFICATE_COMPRESSION and
SSL_OP_NO_RX_CERTIFICATE_COMPRESSION options of the
.Xr SSL_CTX_set_options 3
or
.Xr SSL_set_options 3
functions.
.Pp
.Fn COMP_zlib ,
.Fn COMP_brotli
and
.Fn COMP_zstd
are stream-based compression methods.
Internal state (including compression dictionary) is maintained between
calls.
If an error is returned, the stream is corrupted, and should be closed.
.Pp
.Fn COMP_zlib_oneshot ,
.Fn COMP_brotli_oneshot
and
.Fn COMP_zstd_oneshot
are not stream-based.
These methods do not maintain state between calls.
An error in one call does not affect future calls.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
.Fn COMP_CTX_new
returns a
.Vt COMP_CTX
on success, or NULL on failure.
.Pp
.Fn COMP_CTX_get_method ,
.Fn COMP_zlib ,
.Fn COMP_zlib_oneshot ,
.Fn COMP_brotli ,
.Fn COMP_brotli_oneshot ,
.Fn COMP_zstd ,
and
.Fn COMP_zstd_oneshot
return a
.Vt COMP_METHOD
on success, or NULL on failure.
.Pp
.Fn COMP_CTX_get_type
and
.Fn COMP_get_type
return a NID value.
On failure, NID_undef is returned.
.Pp
.Fn COMP_compress_block
and
.Fn COMP_expand_block
return the number of bytes stored in the output buffer
.Fa out .
This may be 0. On failure, -1 is returned.
.Pp
.Fn COMP_get_name
returns a
.Sy const char *
that must not be freed on success, or NULL on failure.
.Pp
.Fn BIO_f_zlib ,
.Fn BIO_f_brotli
and
.Fn BIO_f_zstd
return NULL on error, and a
.Sy BIO_METHOD
on success.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr BIO_new 3 ,
.Xr SSL_CTX_set_options 3 ,
.Xr SSL_set_options 3
.Sh HISTORY
Brotli and Zstandard functions were added in OpenSSL 3.2.
